From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:22:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/apple-dart: admit the J604's internal display
 DARTs at boot again

On 7.3.0.aurora1-1.701 the J604 stays on the boot framebuffer (simpledrm,
Hyprland "Unknown-1 3024x1890@60"). Both internal display DARTs log
"Leaving inherited display DART untouched; explicit guarded probe
required" and return -ENODEV, so 30ae00000.dcp defers until the deferred
probe timeout (11.2 s) and then fails "inherited SID23 domain not
qualified": dcp_m4_dart_check() finds no retained DART domain on it.

1.617 admitted both DARTs at boot on the J604 through
apple_dart_display_admitted_at_boot() (91facf5bd5, "Admit the J604's
retained display at boot"). The 7.3 integration skipped that hunk as
covered by Aurora's firmware-path display handoff, but Aurora's gate
still requires apple_dart.j713_dcp and apple_dart.j713_display, which an
Omarchy install does not carry.

Restore the board exception on top of Aurora's apple_t8132_firmware_path()
gate. Nothing else changes: off the qualified firmware the DARTs are
still left alone, the frontend mappings and the DCP handoff are still
validated, and the parameters keep working on every board.

Fixes: 5bc1f31f98 ("j604: integrate the J604 series onto Aurora 7.3 (shipping snapshot)")

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
index 3dc77ff8bc..62ee206eea 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
@@ -5055,6 +5055,20 @@ static bool apple_dart_is_available(struct device_node *np)
 	return false;
 }
 
+/*
+ * M4 boards whose internal display DARTs are admitted at boot, without the
+ * j713_dcp and j713_display opt-in the guarded bring-up keeps elsewhere. The
+ * J604 has started its DCP and scanout frontend from the loader's handoff on
+ * every boot since that path was qualified on it, and an Omarchy install
+ * carries neither parameter. Only the gate moves: the frontend mappings and
+ * the DCP handoff are still validated, and without a complete handoff the
+ * DCP and frontend are refused and the boot framebuffer stays.
+ */
+static bool apple_dart_display_admitted_at_boot(void)
+{
+	return of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j604");
+}
+
 static int apple_dart_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	int ret, sid;
@@ -5105,7 +5119,7 @@ static int apple_dart_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (j713_display && !IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_APPLE_DART_J713_DCP))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EOPNOTSUPP,
 				     "retained J713 display requires CONFIG_APPLE_DART_J713_DCP=y\n");
-	if (j713_display &&
+	if (j713_display && !apple_dart_display_admitted_at_boot() &&
 	    ((res->start == 0x30a300000ULL && !READ_ONCE(apple_dart_frontend_enabled)) ||
 	     (res->start == 0x30a340000ULL && !READ_ONCE(apple_dart_dcp_enabled)))) {
 		dev_info(dev, "Leaving inherited display DART untouched; explicit guarded probe required\n");
-- 
